WEBVTT

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.910
The story until now.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:16.430
Nozomu, convinced that this country must change, travels to America to study modern policy.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:22.180
But what awaited him was the harsh racial discrimination of being judged as a viewing-type eroterrorist.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.930
“Wasn't I a viewing-type eroterrorist the second I saw Yingling!?

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.600
By that standard, Japanese middle-school boys are all terrorists!”

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.310
He was told firmly,

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.510
“The American government does not negotiate with terrorists”,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.490
his letter of recommendation was rejected, and he was imprisoned in Alcatraz.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.820
Despairing Nozomu's cellmate,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.190
Bob the academic leftist in a Guevara t-shirt, struck up a conversation.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.880
“After all, the post-Shogunate history of Japan was constructed by Shiba Ryotaro, right?”

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.260
he bluntly proclaimed.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.740
“His white hair is so cool,”

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.780
Nozomu said with all his might.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.970
Good morning, class.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.330
Isn't there something different about him?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.110
His glasses!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:50.440
Keyframers aren't answering their phones anymore

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:50.600
AD isn't reading the storyboards

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:50.770
Production manager lost the cut bag

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:50.940
Finisher is scary

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.100
Art director is scary

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:51.310
Filmer is scary

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.940
To be honest,

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.190
last week I forgot to write scriptures on my glasses,

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.410
so the ghosts took them away.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.300
I don't really get what you mean,

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.370
but you've stopped wearing glasses, right?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.370
Well, I got some disposable contacts,

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.710
so I thought I'd try using those.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.840
That's so not you, Teacher!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.880
I won't accept you like that!

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.880
What's she boiling over about?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.600
Everyone chip in! We're buying Teacher some glasses!

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.810
I'll go buy them!

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.320
Why did you buy tinted glasses like that?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.270
I thought they'd be cute.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.160
Mysterious, if anything.{*}

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.630
Schoolgirls all sell their panties.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.020
What!?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:59.060
The schoolgirls in Shibuya all whore themselves.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.010
Teacher...

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:01.960
You were there?

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.560
Yes, always.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.850
Teacher is wearing tinted glasses.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.570
That's right, when people go by their prejudices and preconceived notions, we call that “wearing tinted glasses”!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.360
Girls with big boobs are dumb.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.580
The ones with dark nipples are kinky.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.770
Oh, so that's what “tinted glasses” means.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:27.060
I always thought it was because of how rosy I felt thinking about boys in glasses.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:29.150
How long have you—!

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.980
Computer janitors are all messing with you.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.910
Bureaucrats are all lazy.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.410
You're blaming the glasses, but isn't he just saying what he wants to?

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.540
It's not Teacher's fault! The tinted glasses are making him say it!

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:41.550
How about this?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.540
Teacher, do you remember what just happened?

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.330
Well...

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.770
You said...

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.840
I said something that horrible!?

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.000
Anime is for little kids.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.360
Temps quit after three months.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.270
Shunsuke doesn't run.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.590
Labor unions are left-wing.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.530
...and stuff!

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:06.780
You didn't say that.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.820
Is it really because of these?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.040
Japs all live in goddamn rabbit hutches.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.840
I knew it.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.660
She always says that kind of thing.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:19.620
Where did you find tinted glasses this dangerous?

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.280
I'll show you.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.450
Welcome.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.760
I'm the owner, Sabae.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.930
What are you doing selling tinted glasses like this!?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.730
They're tinted glasses. Of course they're like that.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:39.440
We have plenty, so feel free to take your time looking.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.720
There are a kind of retro design.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.120
They're early Showa-style tinted glasses.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.740
Back in the kitchen, woman.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.480
They're tinted to that era!?

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.310
Nowadays, only politicians say things like that.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:59.070
These are womens' tinted glasses from the early '90s.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.230
They make her eyebrows look thick!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.300
If he's not rich, tall, or Ivy League, I don't want him.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.220
Are those tinted glasses from the bubble era!?

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.640
There were plenty of tinted glasses back then.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.510
Then again, there are plenty of varieties from every era.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.140
The ones from the war are especially dangerous. Please don't put them on.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.260
Do people buy these tinted glasses?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.620
Thanks to the glasses boom nowadays, they're selling great.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.870
I've taken advantage of it and put out this book.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:35.560
I put together a book of guys

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.120
who look like they look at life through tinted glasses. {*}

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.870
Does that even sell?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.290
Honestly, it hasn't been doing that well.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.800
Hey, some of these are kind of cute!

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.810
Mind if I try them on?

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:47.800
Go right ahead.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.960
Wait! Don't look at yourself!

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:54.030
Creepy nerd.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:57.390
What did I just call myself!?

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.270
That kind of thing happens when you look at yourself with tinted glasses.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.640
Is that how society looks at me!?

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.860
That had a pitiful result.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.020
Maybe I should get myself some trendy tinted glasses.{if he says "yes, always" in the animu i'm going to piss myself laughing}

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.570
Oh, you were there?

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.160
I told you...

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.460
You horny bald bastard.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.030
What did I just say about myself!?

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.710
I told you not to look at yourself with tinted glasses on!

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.710
Hey, these aren't glasses.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.210
Those are tinted headphones.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.540
Huh? What're those?

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:35.680
Tinted headphones impose prejudices on what you hear.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:36.420
How's this?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.240
Those are pretty old headphones.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:47.120
Well, people do have prejudices about music.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.470
Oh, and this is a tinted mouth guard.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.160
It puts your preconceptions on what you taste.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.510
Chain restaurant ramen sucks.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:03.210
Yeah, there are people who think the chains are all bad.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:07.840
As they get older, the tints seem to get lighter.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:12.280
Of course. Back then people didn't have as much information;

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:16.720
as people learn more and more, the tint gets lighter.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:23.550
Even when experts get together and can't decide, sometimes kids get together and figure it out. That kind of thing.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:31.500
Even if you don't buy from me, aren't you all already wearing tinted glasses?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.860
I can see it.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:36.820
That's right.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.460
Now, we must all take off our tinted glasses of prejudice.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.800
Wait, even for that kind of thing!?

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.180
I must.  I must remove my tinted glasses.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.200
It's a whole new emotion...

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.570
No matter how I look at it, you're into that kind of thing.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.720
You're just looking at it through tinted glasses!

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.540
Teachers are all leftists.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:24.900
All of them.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:45.100
Lunchtime is an exciting red black black red yellow black normal black black red reminiscence red black red red

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.280
You got black normal red

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.720
Come on, red black black Nami line

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.500
Man, this's dull.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:51.980
The author

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:52.150
wasn't ready in time

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:52.320
for this to be in a GN.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:52.480
Since we couldn't

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:52.690
get a title page yet,

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:52.900
we made our own.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:09.300
Class has some time off.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.090
Did something happen?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.690
You'll find out when you get older. {lit. "better for a kid not to know", coming back}

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.610
I'm so bored I could die.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.140
That's it! I'll give someone a call!

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:34.640
Hi!

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.540
Hi, Ohkusa, are you doing anything right now?

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.100
Sorry, I'm so busy!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.700
What's up with her?

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.140
Rush work, rush work. {implications of it being wartime}

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.670
That's it, I'll go to karaoke!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.410
Hello?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.340
You're right in your house, right?

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.360
Of course I am, Chiri.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.600
Okay. I'll be checking up on you in an hour.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.480
Feint.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.230
Now I'm too scared to go out!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:26.980
I'm bored.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.790
Unfortunately, you cannot leave your house.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.210
But this place is so cramped!

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:39.460
You yourself wanted to play at being the poor student.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:42.840
That's right.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.880
It's fine as long as I never leave the estate.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.270
I have purchased the neighbors.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.990
Excellent work, Tokita.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:11.040
If I can't leave my house, then I'll simply buy out the neighbors, and add them to my estate!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.780
Ah, how pleasant.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:18.900
You're right in your house, right?

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:22.210
Of course! I'm right in my own room.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.430
I'm not lying, am I?

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:26.350
Of course not.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.610
Wow, there's a shop like that around here?

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:34.980
Ramen...

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.170
What a refreshingly proletarian meal! I simply must have it!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.550
But they don't appear to deliver.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.440
I want it!

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.660
I want it! I want it!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.590
Hold on a moment.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.270
If we simply purchase the neighboring houses in order like this,

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.730
I believe we can reach the ramen joint.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.140
What's this? Such a funny pose.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.780
Is this a new diet?

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.040
It's because you sent my wall flying!

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.360
This is now part of Our estate.{caps for royal we.}

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:37.990
Begone.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.790
What do you mean!?

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:43.050
This is grounds for legal action!

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:47.490
Have your lawyer explain it to you later.

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:49.260
No, explain it to me now!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.520
Is wanting some ramen that bad?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:52.560
Ramen?

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.190
Beat red!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.700
Beat red! Beat red!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.630
Beat red! Beat red!

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.520
Smash red!

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:20.710
If you lift your leg like that, people will see your panties!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.670
Eww, they're staring at me.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:28.280
They're the kind that are supposed to be seen! You're just looking for an excuse to be angry!

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:32.800
Teacher...

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:39.220
He's not looking at me!

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:43.290
Perhaps I should try to find fault.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:44.780
The Komei Shingon, naturally

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:53.700
Lately, people have often do things that are bad ideas specifically to be called out.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:58.360
Like idols who deliberately flash their panties to get their fans' attention!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.990
Politicians who make comments knowing they'll be criticized!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:11.170
Sharapova putting on fake nipples to make people think they can see through!

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:14.000
We can see her nipples!

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.720
I can't see it as anything but deliberate provocation!

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.070
I said Osim.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.070
Blonde pig!

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.070
That's gotta be intentional.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.970
Koike Teppei should play me.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.130
No way!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.040
Oh man, she went for it.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:46.820
That's right, there's a lot of casting choices that make you think they're trolling. {i think i found my metaphor.}

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:52.030
Things like A-bleep-hime must have seemed the same way at the time.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.850
Hey, look at that Miya-bleep Aoi.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.220
too cute!

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.100
Oh no!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.890
Hm, someone's trolling over there too.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:04.100
Our unreleased single leaked onto the net!

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.570
It's such a failure!

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.900
You did it on purpose!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.760
A horrible bug has occured in our program.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:11.740
If you input a certain command,

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.420
the mosaics go away.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.430
Please don't do this.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.990
It's a horrible bug.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.890
You had to have done that on purpose!

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.720
If you fall for that kind of shit, you just lost the game.

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:24.790
Definitely.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:28.650
The best we can do is attempt to determine when someone's intentionally trolling,

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.900
and when they're just naturally provoking.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.840
I couldn't eat my pizza! Give me my money back!

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.710
This is natural...

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:39.520
Of course! No need for a receipt.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.350
And this has to be on purpose.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.890
How about this?

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.250
I'm super-sexy today.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.520
I must be giving off hormones.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.310
The things a ditzy celeb gets wrong!

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.280
They're obviously trolling!

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:55.340
You mustn't spoil them.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:56.870
How about that?

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:01.410
That's right, the weird names people give their kids.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:05.070
Oh well, with him it's gotta be natural.

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:08.320
It's okay to call him out on it, but you might get smacked.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.250
At this point, I'd have to call them all traps.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:13.840
I'm in despair.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:20.680
The amount of deliberate trolling lately has left me in despair!

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:27.270
And now, a troll line dance is starting!

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.590
If I bite, I lose! I've got to run away!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.690
A certain sports newspaper's headline!

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:36.430
If I bite, I lose!

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:40.710
A neon sign that never gets fixed!

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.830
They're just waiting to crack a joke!

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.730
But falling for it even when you know 
someone's trolling is a sign of kindness.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.090
You were there?

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:49.580
Yes, always.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:53.670
Take a look at the MPs chosen to represent the country.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.650
Oh, cup noodles?

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.630
Those are like ¥400, right?

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.560
They're kind enough to take the bait over and over.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.260
Normal people are too busy to do that.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.250
Well, that's for sure.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.290
An idiot trolling or an idiot biting

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:13.460
If they were both idiots, it wouldn't be a troll

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:15.730
What do you mean, Rin?

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.990
The one who's trolling is the one who benefits, right, Brother?

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:23.790
On the other hand, the one being trolled isn't 
even just taking a risk. It's sure they'll get caught.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.970
Like if you get sweet-talked in by a sting operation!

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:28.710
You're under arrest!

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:34.390
Or if you buy in thinking the market's hit bottom, but it finds a second or third bottom!

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:36.390
Why don't you buy in?

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:41.180
Or Kinsei Middle School, pitching just the
way the batter likes it in order to get data!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.190
Or allowing yourself to be attacked as an excuse to get into the war!

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:46.940
How fearsome!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:51.220
Everyone, rather than being caught by trolls,

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.780
you should start trolling to avoid it!

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:55.580
I always have.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.500
I think that just came naturally.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:02.130
But it's even worse when you finally do it and you get ignored.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.920
I'm sure one of our kind readers will bite!

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:06.020
There!

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.460
It may be hard to understand,

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.680
but everyone's trolling a little.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:24.020
Come on, everyone, you aren't lifting your legs high enough!

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.960
Do it higher, like we practiced!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.700
I can't do it any higher!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:29.520
Do it!

00:19:29.740 --> 00:19:32.210
If your body's too stiff, use the sand curse.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:33.560
Don't you know?

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:36.790
It's how they make bodies flexible right after death.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.840
You wash sand from deep in the mountain valleys with pure spring water,

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.290
over the span of a week dry it atop a rock 100 times,

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.950
and chant the incantation while waving a foot-long pomegranate tree wand over the sacred artifact.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.730
Um... hello?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:03.840
That's too high!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.580
There are trolls so deep no one can even bite.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.980
Like Yasuha's faxes...

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.170
All right, everyone, lift them as high as you can!

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:24.610
It's not good! It's so high it can't be grabbed!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:26.010
What are you saying!?

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.130
He caught it!

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.690
You thought no one could catch your leg!

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.030
You were wrong!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:47.730
You were wrong!

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:49.430
You were wrong!

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.720
You were wrong about that!

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:58.020
It's like they're doing it in another dimension. {*}

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:05.830
By the way, usually if a stranger showed up at field
day and grabbed a girl's leg, he'd be arrested, right?

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:44.360
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:46.970
Matching the song, let's draw artistically, okay?

00:22:48.670 --> 00:22:54.170
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.940 --> 00:23:00.990
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:02.450
Lightning...

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:04.210
Flash!

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:05.860
Lightning...

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:07.440
Flash!

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:10.870
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:14.030
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:16.920
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:20.160
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:24.760
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:28.010
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:30.970
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:33.010
Bye bye!
